# Generated from: specs/bug-fix-epic-membership-deadlocking-issue-selection/requirements.md
# Issue: #149
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @start-issue @run-loop @issue-149
Feature: Epic membership does not deadlock issue selection
  Epic membership was previously conflated with execution dependencies, causing
  a ready child to be filtered while its coordination epic remained open.
  Relationship roles must now be classified explicitly without removing the
  identity that downstream epic consumers require.

  @regression
  Scenario: Bare interactive selection keeps a ready epic child actionable
    Given an open epic and an open child linked by both a native parent and "Depends on" reference
    And the child has no open sibling or non-epic prerequisite
    When bare interactive start-issue resolves and filters the candidate set
    Then the child remains actionable while the coordination epic is open
    And closing the epic is not required to start the child

  @regression
  Scenario: Runner selection uses explicit epic semantics
    Given an automatable epic child whose open coordination epic is not automatable
    When manual selection and the SDLC runner evaluate the child's readiness
    Then both selectors classify the epic relationship as non-blocking coordination
    And the runner result does not depend on the epic being absent from its candidate pool

  @regression
  Scenario: Genuine dependencies still block an epic child
    Given an epic child also depends on an open sibling or other non-epic issue
    When manual selection or runner selection evaluates readiness
    Then the child remains blocked by the genuine unresolved issue
    And the diagnostic does not name the open coordination epic as a blocker

  @regression
  Scenario: Downstream epic discovery retains every supported link form
    Given a child uses the current dual-link format, body-only fallback, or native-only link
    When write-spec resolves its umbrella or open-pr resolves its epic siblings
    Then the correct coordination epic is discovered
    And umbrella amendment and sibling-aware version classification continue to work

  @regression
  Scenario: Ambiguous and non-epic parent identity fails safely
    Given a relationship target is confirmed non-epic or its metadata lookup fails
    When readiness is evaluated
    Then the relationship remains an execution dependency and is not silently discarded
    And a metadata failure emits an actionable warning naming the affected relationship

  @regression
  Scenario: Cross-skill regression preserves ordering and epic consumers
    Given a disposable issue graph produced from the current draft-issue epic contract
    When verification exercises bare start-issue, runner selection, parent-spec discovery, and release classification
    Then the first child is selectable while the epic remains open
    And later children remain ordered by real sibling dependencies
    And automated coverage includes native-plus-body, body-only, native-only, non-epic, and metadata-failure cases
